---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionTitle from "../components/SectionTitle.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - FLIPSIGHT"
  description="FLIPSIGHT is an Antwerp-based independent record label and art project built around artists, vinyl, custom artwork and small rooms."
>
  <div class="fs-page fs-page-stack">
    <section class="grid items-end gap-8 md:grid-cols-[5fr_6fr]">
      <div>
        <div class="fs-meta">About</div>
        <h1 class="fs-display mt-4 text-[clamp(50px,7vw,118px)]">Artists,<br />records,<br />rooms.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-6">
        <p class="max-w-xl text-[clamp(18px,2.1vw,28px)] leading-tight text-[var(--fs-ink)]">
          FLIPSIGHT is a small independent record label and art project from Antwerp. We release electronic music on vinyl, build a visual world around each record, and gather people around the sound when it makes sense.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-3 border-t fs-soft-rule pt-4 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[var(--fs-mute)] sm:grid-cols-3">
          <span>Antwerp / 2023</span>
          <span>Vinyl / editions</span>
          <span>Limited runs / real rooms</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[4fr_8fr]">
      <div class="border-t fs-rule pt-5">
        <div class="fs-meta">The release</div>
        <h2 class="fs-display mt-3 text-[clamp(36px,4.8vw,74px)]">Built around the artist.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-8">
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-[clamp(18px,2vw,26px)] leading-tight text-[var(--fs-ink)]">
          Each release starts with the music and the person behind it. We listen, talk, test versions, refine the direction and only then decide how the record should look, feel and exist in the world.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="border-t fs-soft-rule pt-4">
            <div class="fs-meta-muted">01 / Listening</div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
              Selections are made for feeling, function and detail: music that can live at home, in warm-ups, in late rooms and in the hands of people who care.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-t fs-soft-rule pt-4">
            <div class="fs-meta-muted">02 / Direction</div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
              Artwork is made for the record, not dropped on top of it. The palette, sleeve, marks and images are shaped to belong to the sound.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-t fs-soft-rule pt-4">
            <div class="fs-meta-muted">03 / Object</div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
              Most FLIPS releases are pressed in limited runs of 300 copies: physical objects with weight, traces, catalogue numbers and a reason to be kept.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <SectionTitle eyebrow="Practice" title="Sound with its own visual life." note="Vinyl / FLIPSART / editions" />
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[5fr_7fr]">
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
          A FLIPSIGHT record is more than a track on a platform. It is something you can hold, play, look at, file, lend, wear down and keep. That physical side is part of the music, not a nostalgic extra.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
          Around the records, FLIPSIGHT also creates art pieces, prints and FLIPSART editions. Some works grow directly out of a release, others come from the wider visual archive of the label.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-8 border-y fs-rule py-8 md:grid-cols-[4fr_6fr]">
      <div>
        <div class="fs-meta-muted">Community</div>
        <h2 class="fs-display mt-3 text-[clamp(32px,4vw,58px)]">Into rooms.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-5">
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
          Label nights, FLIPSIGHT Cafés, listening moments and vernissages are our way of bringing the catalogue off the screen. Small rooms, good systems, familiar faces, new people, records on the table.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-ink-2)]">
          At its core, FLIPSIGHT is simple: good music, strong visuals, real objects and honest collaboration.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-2">
          <a class="fs-meta border fs-soft-rule px-4 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-[var(--fs-ink)] hover:bg-[var(--fs-bg-2)]" href="/music">Music</a>
          <a class="fs-meta border fs-soft-rule px-4 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-[var(--fs-ink)] hover:bg-[var(--fs-bg-2)]" href="/art">FLIPSART</a>
          <a class="fs-meta border fs-soft-rule px-4 py-3 transition-colors hover:border-[var(--fs-ink)] hover:bg-[var(--fs-bg-2)]" href="/events">Events</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[4fr_8fr]">
      <div>
        <div class="fs-meta-muted">A small note</div>
      </div>
      <p class="max-w-3xl border-t fs-soft-rule pt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--fs-mute)]">
        FLIPSIGHT was started in Antwerp in 2023 by C. de Boer, also known as Chris Farmer, and F. Lagrange. Chris takes care of the music side; F. handles the visual direction and the web. The label is not really about us, though. It is about the records, the artists and the people who keep showing up around them.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
